    },
    {
      "id": "the-first-part-of-henry-the-sixth/sceneI_12.5/p@41025",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "TALBOT.\nMy thoughts are whirled like a potter’s wheel;\nI know not where I am, nor what I do.\nA witch by fear, not force, like Hannibal,\nDrives back our troops and conquers as she lists.\nSo bees with smoke and doves with noisome stench\nAre from their hives and houses driven away.\nThey call’d us for our fierceness, English dogs;\nNow like to whelps we crying run away.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-first-part-of-henry-the-sixth/sceneI_12.5/p@41025/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 7,
